  "verify": "Pins from Waveshare's demo code and schematic (https://github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75). 1) pin_config.h carries two sets of audio macros. The '// ES8311' block says I2S_MCK_IO 16 - wrong: GPIO16 is header pin, MCLK is GPIO42 in the schematic, in the BSP and in the second block (MCLKPIN 42) that 08_ES8311.ino really uses. The names DOPIN 10 / DIPIN 8 are from the codec's side: the sketch passes DIPIN as the ESP's data out. Believed the schematic and the BSP: ESP out 8, ESP in 10, MCLK 42. On the board and not in this preset: LC76G: no driver. Brightness is a command to the panel, not a backlight pin. Compiled; not run on a board here.",
